  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "Scope mismatch: the estimand requires the fraction among ALL new customers reached by paid search, but the analyst restricted the denominator to only those with status='completed', excluding other new paid_search customers.",
    "False premise handling: one of the required premises ('converted' means completed checkout) is violated (21 rows), yet the analyst did not refuse to answer as required.",
    "Denominator bias: by dropping non‑completed rows, the conversion rate is computed on a reduced set, inflating the fraction relative to the true population."
